 fm=['This section introduces','The EBM can be learned','The first term','Then, the Monte Carlo','Thus, the loss','Let $\\theta','To enable','In implementation']
 block('ebm-normalization','F',fm[0],fm[1],[18,19]);block('ebm-mle','F',fm[1],fm[2],[19]);block('ebm-langevin','F',fm[2],fm[3],[19]);block('ebm-sampling-loss','F',fm[3],fm[4],[19])
 new('prefix-coinfo-main','正文Property2：三元信息随前缀增加','Main Property 2: information increases with gate prefixes','Property2; Eq.(11)',r'I(X;\Sigma_{1:l};Y)\le I(X;\Sigma_{1:l+1};Y)',[4,14])
 source('prefix-coinfo-main','B.2',get('prefix-coinfo')['original_proof_md'],[14],r'Property 2. If the DNN does not introduce additional complexity that is not caused by the input, then the complexity increases along with the number of gating layers. The three complexities defined in this section are $H(\Sigma)$, $I(X;\Sigma)$, and $I(X;\Sigma;Y)$.')
