 new('tc-zero-independence','总相关为0当且仅当门坐标独立','Zero total correlation iff gate coordinates are independent','Section4.1 unnumbered property',r'TC(\Sigma_l)=0\Longleftrightarrow p(\sigma_l)=\prod_dp(\sigma_l^d)',[5])
 get('tc-zero-independence')['original_statement_md']=r'For gating states of the $l$-th layer, $TC(\Sigma_l)$ measures dependence between gating states in different dimensions. Specifically, $TC(\Sigma_l)=KL(p(\sigma_l)\Vert\prod_dp(\sigma_l^d))$, with $p(\sigma_{l,d})\sim\operatorname{Bernoulli}(a_{l,d})$. In particular, $TC(\Sigma_l)$ is zero if and only if all dimensions of $\sigma_l$ are independent with each other. In this case, we say all dimensions in $\Sigma_l$ are disentangled.'
 spec('tc-zero-independence',finite_ass,[LAW,TC],[step('证明KL等号条件','Prove the equality condition for KL',r'Gibbs逐项余量$p\log(p/q)-p+q$非负；当p≠q时严格正，包括p=0,q>0情形。总和等于KL，因为两律总质量都1。所以KL=0迫使每个原子p=q；反向逐项p=q给KL=0。',r'The Gibbs remainder $p\log(p/q)-p+q$ is nonnegative, and strictly positive when p≠q, including p=0,q>0. Its sum equals KL because both laws have mass one. Thus KL zero forces equality at every atom; conversely equal atoms give KL zero.',r'D_{KL}(p\Vert q)=0\Longleftrightarrow p=q',['gibbs_term_strict','divergence_zero_iff']),step('代入真实边缘乘积','Use the actual marginal product',r'边缘乘积$q=\prod_dp_d$已由真实边缘构造并证明正规；正联合原子保证q也正。上述KL等号条件给$p=\prod_dp_d$，这正是有限门坐标的联合独立性定义。',r'The product $q=\prod_dp_d$ is constructed from the actual marginals and is normalized. Positive joint atoms have positive q. The KL equality condition gives $p=\prod_dp_d$, precisely joint independence of finite gate coordinates.',r'TC(p)=0\Longleftrightarrow p=\prod_dp_d',['productCoordinateLaw','product_coordinate_support','total_correlation_zero_iff_independent'])],('完整验证原未编号TC=0 iff所有坐标联合独立，包含零概率状态和确定性坐标。','The complete unnumbered TC=0 iff joint coordinate independence property is verified, including zero-probability states and deterministic coordinates.'))
 new('regularizer-definition','复杂度正则化目标定义','Complexity-regularized objective definition','Eq.(4); Eq.(30)',r'\mathcal L=\mathcal L_{task}+\lambda\sum_{l=1}^LH(\Sigma_l)',[7,18],'definition')
